@* Global pixel-space background scenario, shared by /, /staking and
   /procurement-lab (all StakingLayout pages).

   The permanent base — cross-shaped stars, the Andromeda galaxy and the two
   planets, plus the Ethereum/Solana/BNB chain badges — never changes between
   routes. Both containers carry data-permanent, so Blazor's enhanced
   navigation keeps these exact DOM nodes across route changes and the sky's
   animations never restart; the random palette variant is also picked once
   per visit instead of re-rolling on every navigation.

   Per-route dressing lives in .gs-layer wrappers: the home layer (catalog
   coffee bags, scattered coins and the pixel crew) and the staking layer
   (the drifting coffee coins). Which layer is visible is driven by the
   data-scene-route attribute that App.razor renders on <html>; visibility
   rules for that attribute live in app.css (CSS isolation cannot select
   outside this component), while the layers' own styles and transitions are
   in GlobalScene.razor.css. Only the class/attribute that selects layers
   changes on a route switch, so the outgoing design fades out over the
   preserved base while the incoming one fades in.

   The crew robots render in the second fixed container which stacks ABOVE
   the page content: they must stay pointer-reachable (they are draggable,
   and pixelCrewRuntime.js hit-tests them) even though the space itself is a
   background. pointer-events: none on the wrapper with pointer-events: auto
   on each robot means only the robots intercept input. Everything else —
   stars, planets, badges, bags, coins — stays beneath @Body.

   The crew is not choreographed: wwwroot/js/pixelCrewRuntime.js still mounts
   on the stable #ph-scene-root id (this background container, falling back
   to the whole root as its scene) and drives the robots in the -over
   container; the CSS keyframes remain the no-JS and reduced-motion fallback. *@

<div class="gs-scene gs-scene--bg-@_bgVariant" id="ph-scene-root" data-permanent aria-hidden="true">
    @* Base sky: cross-shaped pixel stars, irregular via per-star custom
       properties. Sixteen of them, dispersed over the whole sky. *@
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--one"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--two"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--three"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--four"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--five"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--six"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--seven"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--eight"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--nine"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--ten"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--eleven"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--twelve"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--thirteen"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--fourteen"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--fifteen"></span>
    <span class="ph-star ph-star--sixteen"></span>

    @* Andromeda, sitting furthest back of anything in the scene: dimmed and
       small enough to read as deep sky rather than as another prop. Sprite
       from tools/generate_andromeda.py. *@
    <img class="ph-sky__andromeda" src="images/pl-andromeda.png" alt="" width="132" height="84" />

    <img class="ph-sky__planet" src="images/pl-planet.png" alt="" />
    <img class="ph-sky__planet ph-sky__planet--ringed" src="images/pl-planet-ringed.png" alt="" />

    @* Pixel chain badges — Ethereum octahedron, Solana stripes, BNB diamonds —
       dim and drifting in the background behind the coins and the crew. Two of
       each, dispersed over the space; the -b variants drop out on narrow
       viewports. *@
    <span class="ph-chain ph-chain--eth-a"><img src="images/pl-chain-ethereum.png" alt="" /></span>
    <span class="ph-chain ph-chain--sol-a"><img src="images/pl-chain-solana.png" alt="" /></span>
    <span class="ph-chain ph-chain--bnb-a"><img src="images/pl-chain-bnb.png" alt="" /></span>
    <span class="ph-chain ph-chain--eth-b"><img src="images/pl-chain-ethereum.png" alt="" /></span>
    <span class="ph-chain ph-chain--sol-b"><img src="images/pl-chain-solana.png" alt="" /></span>
    <span class="ph-chain ph-chain--bnb-b"><img src="images/pl-chain-bnb.png" alt="" /></span>

    @* Staking layer: the drifting coffee coins that used to live inside the
       /staking intro. The layer fades in on /staking and out again everywhere
       else; the vignette ::after keeps the tokens softly dimmed at the edges. *@
    <div class="gs-layer gs-layer--staking">
        <img class="staking-space__coin staking-space__coin--one" src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" />
        <img class="staking-space__coin staking-space__coin--two" src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" />
        <img class="staking-space__coin staking-space__coin--three" src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" />
        <img class="staking-space__coin staking-space__coin--four" src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" />
        <img class="staking-space__coin staking-space__coin--five" src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" />
        <img class="staking-space__coin staking-space__coin--six" src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" />
        <img class="staking-space__coin staking-space__coin--seven" src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" />
    </div>

    @* Home layer, under-content half: the six catalog bags, one per product
       on /products, cut down to tiny pl-bag sprites (tools/generate_pixel_bags.py),
       plus seven coins. The crew runtime owns their positions once it loads —
       they are scattered by the simulation and respawn wherever it decides. The
       coordinates in the stylesheet are the no-JS fallback composition. *@
    <div class="gs-layer gs-layer--home">
        <span class="ph-bag ph-bag--colombia"><img src="images/pl-bag-colombia.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-bag ph-bag--costa-rica"><img src="images/pl-bag-costa-rica.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-bag ph-bag--ethiopia"><img src="images/pl-bag-ethiopia.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-bag ph-bag--guatemala"><img src="images/pl-bag-guatemala.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-bag ph-bag--mexico"><img src="images/pl-bag-mexico.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-bag ph-bag--peru"><img src="images/pl-bag-peru.png" alt="" /></span>

        <span class="ph-coinbit ph-coinbit--ambient-a"><img src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-coinbit ph-coinbit--ambient-b"><img src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-coinbit ph-coinbit--ambient-c"><img src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-coinbit ph-coinbit--loot-scout"><img src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-coinbit ph-coinbit--loot-buyer"><img src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-coinbit ph-coinbit--loot-courier"><img src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" /></span>
        <span class="ph-coinbit ph-coinbit--loot-inspector"><img src="images/coffee-coin-pixel.png" alt="" /></span>
    </div>
</div>

@* Home layer, above-content half: the crew itself. Each roam wrapper is one
   simulated agent; the trained policy in wwwroot/js/pixelCrewPolicy.js picks
   its acceleration every frame from what it can see, and pixelCrewRuntime.js
   writes the result as a transform. Empty hands — they gather, they don't
   work. Drag one anywhere: the policy picks up from the new spot. *@
<div class="gs-crew" id="ph-scene-root-over" data-permanent aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="gs-layer gs-layer--home">
        <div class="ph-scene__roam ph-scene__roam--scout">
            <div class="ph-scene__unit ph-scene__unit--scout">
                <span class="ph-scene__actor ph-scene__actor--scout"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__grab"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__sip"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__plus"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-scene__roam ph-scene__roam--buyer">
            <div class="ph-scene__unit ph-scene__unit--buyer">
                <span class="ph-scene__actor ph-scene__actor--buyer"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__grab"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__sip"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__plus"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-scene__roam ph-scene__roam--courier">
            <div class="ph-scene__unit ph-scene__unit--courier">
                <span class="ph-scene__actor ph-scene__actor--courier"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__grab"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__sip"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__plus"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-scene__roam ph-scene__roam--inspector">
            <div class="ph-scene__unit ph-scene__unit--inspector">
                <span class="ph-scene__actor ph-scene__actor--inspector"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__grab"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__sip"></span>
                <span class="ph-scene__plus"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    // One of the five space palettes per session. The containers are
    // data-permanent, so whichever variant the first full render picked
    // survives every subsequent enhanced navigation — a route change no
    // longer re-rolls the sky, only a fresh full-page load does.
    private readonly int _bgVariant = Random.Shared.Next(5);
}
